        "original_id": "a96ec56c-05d1-5ade-aa51-982a755afbb9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Lesquerella, Thujopsis, Paysonia\n- Plant families: Cupressaceae\n- Chemicals: Lesquerolic acid\n- Concepts: genus reclassification, genetic and morphological features\n\nFacts:\n- Lesquerella is the former name of a genus of flowering plants.\n- Thujopsis is a conifer in the cypress family Cupressaceae, and Thujopsis dolabrata is the sole member of the genus Thujopsis.\n- Until 2002, Paysonia was considered part of the genus Lesquerella, but it was separated based on genetic and morphological features.\n- Lesquerolic acid is a hydroxy acid that occurs naturally in Paysonia lasiocarpa and other Paysonia and Physaria species.",
